{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791727862,"nonce":"UN9AjKs0t99I0JvDBAm8zJi28sM=","title":"text-overflow: ellipsis and line-clamp","message":"Text that does not fit wraps or overflows; there is no ellipsis and no line clamp, which every list row, card title and table cell needs.\n\nWhere: blinc_abi text layout. A single line with overflow other than visible and text-overflow: ellipsis is shaped to the box width less an ellipsis glyph's advance, then ends with one. -webkit-line-clamp/line-clamp: N keeps N lines and ellipsizes the last. Measurement must report the clamped height.\n\nThe other SDK lacks both. ff2f7ff listed them as the remaining paint gaps.\n\nTests: ellipsis at 1x and 2x with proportional and monospace fonts; a clamp of 2 and 3 lines; RTL later; resizing re-ellipsizes; the full text stays in textContent.","files":null}]}